{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Correction: this ticket is UNOWNED, and its AC1 is now unsatisfiable as written\n\nTwo corrections after verifying against the live store and origin/main tip ee2c54f881d6.\n\n**1. Nobody owns this.** status `open`, assignee `null`, claim `null`, zero comments. I had\nbeen treating it as another session's work; that was wrong. The only inbound reference is epic\n78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86 (\"Janitor Cleanup 2026-08-29\") which `depends_on` it — an epic-level\ndependency, not an active worker.\n\n**2. Its premise is largely moot on main, so it needs a RESCOPE before any dispatch.**\n`.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml` and `scripts/install_review_scanners.py` are both\nABSENT from origin/main — reverted by 9c7d78127696. Approach step 1 (guard the\nscanner-integration step) therefore has no file to edit, and **AC1 is unsatisfiable as written**.\n\nWhat SURVIVES and is still valuable: approach steps 2 and 3. Both\n`tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` and `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`\nare present on main. The underlying concern — that a lane can cast a vote without having actually\nexecuted the thing it claims to verify — is real and unaddressed, and it is the same\n\"absence of execution reported as success\" class that has now recurred repeatedly here (9a17's\nworker kill, 1ef8's vacuously-passing AC3, docker-storage-cap reporting a cap 'in effect' after a\nSIGHUP that does not apply it).\n\n**3. file_impact is EMPTY**, so a rebar-implement dispatch would refuse anyway.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nDo NOT dispatch a fix agent. Rescope first: rewrite AC1 against what exists on main today, decide\nwhether the scanner-integration lane is coming back (which interacts with ticket\nfloppy-patriotic-unau's re-land strategy — that ticket's own ACs are ALSO stale, describing change\n2612 which was landed and then reverted), and record a non-empty file_impact. Those two tickets are\nsequential, not parallel.\n\nRelatedly, a NEW ticket filed tonight covers an adjacent instance of the same class:\ntrustful-combative-grackle (9c64-7582-ffad-4fea) — nothing ties test.yml's sweep-lane extras to the\ngating lane's, and `test_ci_workflow_parity.py` was edited by the very commit that diverged them\nwithout catching it. If this ticket is rescoped around parity-checks-that-do-not-check, the two\nshould be read together."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788547315713951001,"uuid":"0dd60676-a65f-485e-b1db-a52f40b21d68"}